From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Implement IXMLDOMParseError::get_filepos.

AI-assisted (Claude), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream.

Windows 10 (msxml3 and msxml6, x86_64 and i686, measured with
docs/wine-repro/msxml3-parseerror-filepos/measure.c, 2026-11-08):
get_filepos returns S_FALSE and 0 when the document has no parse error
(new document, after a successful loadXML), like get_errorCode, get_line,
get_linepos and get_reason; with a parse error it returns S_OK and the
offset of the offending character (0 after loadXML(""), 8 for
"<a><b></a>"); a NULL pointer gives E_INVALIDARG.

Wine returned E_NOTIMPL. SOLIDWORKS calls get_filepos after loadXML("")
fails, and the E_NOTIMPL preceded its C++ exception.

The change is limited to get_filepos: Wine does not record error positions
(filepos stays 0, marked todo_wine), and get_line and get_linepos, which
still return S_OK without an error, are left as they are (get_errorCode
and get_reason already return S_FALSE then).

v2 (2026-11-08): v1 returned S_OK also without a parse error; its own
test failed on Windows 10 (L1). Returns S_FALSE then, and the test covers
the loadXML("") and malformed-XML cases measured on Windows.

v2 revised (2026-11-09, after cross review): the new checks run on
DOMDocument30 and DOMDocument60, the classes measured, with a new
document for every load as in the measurement, and cover all measured
states: new document, loadXML(""), "<a><b></a>" (8), an error on the
third line (12) and a successful load; NULL is checked in each state.

v2 revised (2026-11-09, after L2 run 42552802374): Wine's loadXML("")
returned S_FALSE without recording a parse error, so get_filepos (and
get_errorCode) reported no error there, where Windows reports
0xc00ce558 (XML_E_MISSINGROOT) and get_filepos returns S_OK - the
SOLIDWORKS case. loadXML of an empty string now records that code; a
NULL string is left as it was (not measured).

--- a/dlls/msxml3/domdoc.c
